      <activity id="84c9c1b7-0775-5849-9e72-da73951a7afb" activityNameId="a9ca255f-cc74-5d17-8838-c686c4110128" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipe [998f258541]</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, residential, by conversion of hydrogen using fuel cell, PEM, allocated by exergy, distributed by pipeline, produced by Pyrolysis using natural gas from Switzerland
This dataset represents the supply of 1 megajoule of heat in a residence, by hydrogen conversion in a fuel cell, PEM. The hydrogen is produced by  Pyrolysis, with natural gas from Switzerland as feedstock. Heat conversion efficiency [% LHV input]: 50%. LHV [MJ/kg]: 120. Market price [Euro/MJ]: 0.03. Synthesis efficiency [% LHV input]: 0%. Total cap. Input-related [kW]: 2.74. CO2 biogenic share [%]: 0%. Power [kW]: 1.6. Lifetime [years]: 4.88. Annual operation [hours]: 4100. Allocation factor: 0.12. On-site storage loss [%]: 0. Use loss [%]: 0.56. For more information, refer to: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023. Source: Sacchi, R. and Bauer, C. LCA of Power-to-X processes and applications in the residential sector. Paul Scherrer Institut, 2023.

 UUID: 9624ec7a-486e-311b-8d4d-431d83a91666
Location: 
Technology: 
Time period: 
Production volume: 
Sampling: Sampling procedure: Literature data
Extrapolations: 
Uncertainty adjustments: 
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_9624ec7a-486e-311b-8d4d-431d83a91666.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
